<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><%= csrf_meta_tags %><title>Buzz Buzz · A little awareness goes a long way</title><meta name="description" content="Interactive Buzz Buzz posture awareness demo with simulated wearable telemetry and saved session history."><link rel="stylesheet" href="/demo.css"><script type="module" src="/demo.js"></script></head>
<body><header><a class="brand" href="/"><span class="bee">✳</span> buzz buzz<span class="brand-dot">.</span></a><nav><a href="#today">Overview</a><a href="#history">Your week</a><a href="#guide">Demo guide</a></nav><span class="pill">HACKGT 13 · DEMO</span></header>
<main><div class="intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">SMALL CHECK-INS. BETTER AWARENESS.</p><h1>Find your happy posture.</h1><p>A little nudge to notice how you sit. One session at a time.</p></div><span class="date" id="date"></span></div>
<div class="demo-banner"><span><strong>Simulated wearable</strong> · All readings and history on this page are synthetic.</span><span>Rails + SQLite · saved locally</span></div>
<div id="alert" role="alert" hidden></div>
<section class="top-grid"><article class="live panel"><div class="panel-heading"><p class="eyebrow">YOUR LIVE SESSION</p><span class="status" id="connection">Disconnected</span></div><div class="live-body"><div class="posture-figure" id="figure"><div class="orbit"></div><div class="person"><i class="head"></i><i class="back"></i><i class="legs"></i></div><span class="spark">✦</span></div><div><p class="state-label" id="state-label">Ready when you are</p><h2 id="posture">Make space<br>for a check-in.</h2><p id="state-copy">Connect the simulator to see the wearable’s calculated results.</p></div></div><div class="session-stats"><div><span>Tracked time</span><strong id="live-tracked">00:00</strong></div><div><span>Slouch time</span><strong id="live-slouch">00:00</strong></div><div><span>Episodes</span><strong id="live-episodes">0</strong></div></div><div class="actions"><button class="primary" id="connect">Connect simulator ↗</button><span id="save-status" role="status">No session yet</span></div></article>
<article class="challenge panel"><div class="panel-heading"><p class="eyebrow">TODAY’S LITTLE WIN</p><span class="flower">✺</span></div><span class="points" id="points">+50 points</span><h2>Show up for<br>20 minutes.</h2><p>Awareness starts with showing up. Track a little time and earn your daily bloom.</p><div class="progress-label"><strong id="challenge-progress">0 / 20 min</strong><span id="challenge-percent">0%</span></div><progress id="progress" max="1200" value="0">0%</progress><p class="small" id="reward-copy">One reward per first-seen date. Every check-in counts.</p></article></section>
<section id="today"><div class="section-title"><h2>A snapshot of today</h2><span id="today-caption">Your recorded sessions</span></div><div class="metrics"><article class="panel metric"><span>Total tracked</span><strong id="total-tracked">0 min</strong><small>Time classified by the device</small></article><article class="panel metric"><span>Non-slouch time</span><strong id="non-slouch">—</strong><small>Device-classified, of tracked time</small></article><article class="panel metric"><span>Slouch duration</span><strong id="total-slouch">0 min</strong><small>Time in detected episodes</small></article><article class="panel metric"><span>Slouch episodes</span><strong id="episodes">0</strong><small>Notice patterns, without judgment</small></article></div></section>
<section class="bottom-grid"><article class="panel" id="history"><div class="panel-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE BIGGER PICTURE</p><h2>Your week, in little moments.</h2></div><button class="text-button" id="seed">Load sample week ↗</button></div><p class="small">Sessions by first-seen date · <span id="timezone"></span></p><div class="legend"><span>● Non-slouch</span><span>● Slouch</span></div><div id="chart" class="chart" aria-label="Weekly tracked and slouch time"></div><details><summary>View exact weekly totals</summary><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Date</th><th>Tracked</th><th>Slouch</th><th>Episodes</th></tr></thead><tbody id="weekly-table"></tbody></table></div></details></article>
<article class="panel lab"><p class="eyebrow">PRESENTER CONTROLS</p><h2>Meet your virtual wearable.</h2><p class="small">These controls simulate device-side actions. The dashboard never classifies raw sensor readings.</p><div class="control-grid"><button id="start">Start / calibrate</button><button data-state="upright">Sit upright</button><button data-state="slouching">Sustained slouch</button><button data-state="sensor_error">Sensor error</button><button id="end">End session</button><button id="replay">Replay last packet</button></div><label class="speed">Simulation speed<select id="speed"><option value="1">1× real time</option><option value="30" selected>30× presentation</option><option value="60">60× fast forward</option></select></label><div class="toggles"><label><input type="checkbox" id="offline"> Simulate saving outage</label><label><input type="checkbox" id="pause"> Pause BLE heartbeats</label></div><button class="primary full" id="tour">Run guided demo · ~50 sec</button><p id="tour-status" class="small" role="status">Or explore manually with the controls above.</p></article></section>
<section class="panel sessions"><div class="panel-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">SAVED IN RAILS</p><h2>Your session journal</h2></div><button class="text-button" id="export">Export JSON ↓</button></div><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Session</th><th>First seen</th><th>Tracked</th><th>Slouch</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody id="sessions"></tbody></table></div><p class="small">Open sessions are partial observations. A lost connection does not end a session.</p></section>
<section class="guide" id="guide"><p class="eyebrow">THE 3-MINUTE STORY</p><h2>A wearable that does the thinking.<br>A dashboard that makes it clear.</h2><div class="guide-grid"><div><b>01 / Notice</b><p>The ESP32 will calibrate, classify posture, and time episodes locally. This demo supplies synthetic calculated packets in the proposed 20-byte BLE format.</p></div><div><b>02 / Understand</b><p>The browser decodes results. Rails saves cumulative revisions, so reconnects and repeated transfers don’t multiply your activity.</p></div><div><b>03 / Build awareness</b><p>Review saved time, a sample week, and one daily challenge. Refresh to show persistence. No data is different from zero activity.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="panel posture-context" aria-labelledby="posture-context-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">UNDERSTAND THE PATTERN</p>
  <h2 id="posture-context-title">Why pay attention to slouching?</h2>
  <p class="posture-intro">Long stretches in the same position can leave you feeling stiff or uncomfortable. A sustained slouch can aggravate neck or back discomfort for some people, especially when your desk setup makes it hard to move comfortably.</p>
  <div class="posture-tips">
    <div><h3>Time matters</h3><p>A brief lean is normal. Use your recorded slouch time as a cue to check in and change position, rather than trying to hold yourself rigidly upright.</p></div>
    <div><h3>Make room to move</h3><p>Break up long sitting periods with light activity. Adjust your chair and screen so you can sit comfortably with your back supported.</p></div>
    <div><h3>Your numbers need context</h3><p>A slouch reading describes a detected position. It cannot tell whether you are in pain or whether your back is being harmed. There is no single perfect posture.</p></div>
  </div>
  <p class="posture-sources">Learn more: <a href="https://www.cuh.nhs.uk/patient-information/seating-and-ergonomics/">NHS seating guidance</a> · <a href="https://www.cuh.nhs.uk/patient-information/myth-busting-about-posture-core-stability-and-lifting/">Posture and pain</a> · <a href="https://www.nhs.uk/live-well/exercise/why-sitting-too-much-is-bad-for-us/">Breaking up sitting time</a></p>
</section>
<section class="panel muse-sample" aria-labelledby="muse-sample-title">
  <div class="section-top"><div><p class="eyebrow">A SMALL NEXT STEP</p><h2 id="muse-sample-title">A check-in with Muse</h2></div><span class="subtle-label">Sample conversation · scripted</span></div>
  <p class="muse-sample-intro">An example of turning a posture pattern into a practical habit. These messages are illustrative, not an analysis of your readings or a live Muse response.</p>
  <ol class="muse-messages" aria-label="Sample conversation with Muse">
    <li class="muse-message muse-message-user"><span class="muse-speaker">You</span><p>I keep slouching when I’m studying. Is that bad for my back?</p></li>
    <li class="muse-message"><span class="muse-speaker">Muse</span><p>Slouching sometimes is normal, and a posture reading alone doesn’t mean damage. Staying in one position for a long time can feel uncomfortable. How does your neck or back feel, and when do you notice yourself leaning forward?</p></li>
    <li class="muse-message muse-message-user"><span class="muse-speaker">You</span><p>My neck gets stiff when I lean toward my laptop during long coding sessions.</p></li>
    <li class="muse-message"><span class="muse-speaker">Muse</span><p>Try a small reset: change position, take a short walk if comfortable, and bring the screen to a height and distance that lets you relax. A laptop stand with a separate keyboard and mouse may help. For your next study block, use a pause between tasks as a movement reminder. If the discomfort persists or worsens, check with a healthcare professional.</p></li>
  </ol>

</section>

<footer><span>Made for small moments of awareness. ✳ buzzbuzzlovers</span><button class="text-button" id="reset">Clear simulated history</button><p>Posture-awareness prototype. Hardware sensing, physical vibration, and real BLE pairing are not implemented in this demo. No medical outcomes are claimed.</p></footer></main></body></html>
